From ba733d7f2e3d49e2aefd1dbb71a3633de7a75738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garpur Hnefill Emiliuson <garpurhnefill.emiliuson.d47@mail.toshiba>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:19:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1366/1368] PM: domains: Mark
 dev_pm_domain_allow_detach_on_unbind_cleanup() as inline

Building with CONFIG_PM=n and CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT=y triggers a
-Wunused-function warning for the stub implementation of
dev_pm_domain_allow_detach_on_unbind_cleanup() in pm_domain.h.

This issue only affects the -cip tree. Unlike the surrounding stub
helpers, this function was not declared inline. Mark the stub
implementation as inline so unused configurations do not trigger
compiler warnings.

Fixes: f7c0934b4cc9 ("PM: domains: Add helper to check for PM domain detach on unbind cleanup")
Signed-off-by: Garpur Hnefill Emiliuson <garpurhnefill.emiliuson.d47@mail.toshiba>
Reviewed-by: Nobuhiro Iwamatsu <nobuhiro.iwamatsu.x90@mail.toshiba>
Reviewed-by: Pavel Machek <pavel@nabladev.com>
Signed-off-by: Nobuhiro Iwamatsu <nobuhiro.iwamatsu.x90@mail.toshiba>
---
 include/linux/pm_domain.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/pm_domain.h b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
index 4dd882877ee8..719e501ed282 100644
--- a/include/linux/pm_domain.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
@@ -546,7 +546,7 @@ static inline int dev_pm_domain_set_performance_state(struct device *dev,
 {
 	return 0;
 }
-static bool dev_pm_domain_allow_detach_on_unbind_cleanup(void)
+static inline bool dev_pm_domain_allow_detach_on_unbind_cleanup(void)
 {
 	return false;
 }
